    summary: "A simple outline helps us share clearly. This lesson studies Genesis 1:26-27, Romans 3:23 and 6:23, Isaiah 59:2, Romans 5:8 and John 1:12 and Ephesians 2:8-9 to present God as holy Creator, humanity as sinful and separated, Christ as the substitute who died and rose, and our response of repentance and faith, with attention to the qualities of a clear and gracious presentation.",
